\",\"hypotheses\":[\"X is a topological space.\",\"X is Hausdorff.\",\"K is compact.\"],\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"library/M018-0019/library-sources.json\",\"sha256\":\"388d0738599bce28a7c9ac059f858531d8bc830ecb41a602c6e87d137215847b\"}]}}},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/1/inputs\",\"value\":[\"H003\",\"M001\",\"M016\",\"M013\",\"M014\",\"M018\"]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/1/argument/0/uses\",\"value\":[\"H003\",\"M016\",\"M018\"]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/1/argument/1/uses\",\"value\":[\"M001\",\"M013\",\"M014\",\"M018\"]},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/1/argument/1/text\",\"value\":\"Choose R₀ using F001 and define Q=∏_{i=1}^n[-R₀,R₀]. Each coordinate has absolute value at most ‖x‖, hence K⊆Q. M013 and M014 give μ(Q)=∏_{i=1}^n μ([-R₀,R₀])=(2R₀)^n<∞. Apply M018 to the compact K in the Hausdorff Euclidean space to conclude K is closed and hence Borel measurable; monotonicity yields μ(K)≤μ(Q)<∞. As K was arbitrary, Lebesgue measure is finite on compact sets. The Borel measurable structure on ℝⁿ is the σ-algebra generated by Euclidean opens, so opens are measurable. Joint smoothness and u=q on the open spatial complement of C throughout J imply all first spatial and time derivatives, and the second and mixed derivatives entering e_t, vanish outside C. Thus e(·,t) is continuous with compact support in C. Apply M001 to conclude e(·,t) is integrable. The same smoothness/support argument shows u_t(·,s), u_{x_j}(·,s), e(·,s), and e_t(·,s) are continuous and vanish off C for each s∈J and j=1,…,n. This proves the claimed output for arbitrary t>0.\"},{\"op\":\"replace\",\"path\":\"/graph/inferences/1/applications\",\"value\":[{\"input\":\"M001\",\"at\":\"S002\",\"bindings\":\"X=ℝⁿ with its Euclidean topology and Borel measurable space, V=ℝ, μ=Lebesgue measure, f=e(·,t).\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"ℝⁿ has a measurable space and Euclidean topology.\",\"Its Borel measurable space makes Euclidean opens measurable.\",\"ℝ is a normed additive commutative group.\",\"S001–S002 prove Lebesgue measure is finite on every compact subset of ℝⁿ.\",\"e(·,t) is continuous and has compact support in C by smoothness and H003.\"]},{\"input\":\"M016\",\"at\":\"S001\",\"bindings\":\"X=ℝⁿ with its Euclidean pseudometric; K is an arbitrary compact subset fixed in S001.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"ℝⁿ carries the Euclidean pseudometric.\",\"K is compact by the local arbitrary declaration in S001.\"]},{\"input\":\"M013\",\"at\":\"S002\",\"bindings\":\"ι=Fin n, α(i)=ℝ, s(i)=[−R₀,R₀] for each i.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"Fin n is finite because n is a positive integer.\",\"Each coordinate ℝ is a measure space and its volume measure is sigma-finite.\"]},{\"input\":\"M014\",\"at\":\"S002\",\"bindings\":\"a=−R₀ and b=R₀.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"a and b are real numbers; the source theorem has no additional hypotheses.\"]},{\"input\":\"M018\",\"at\":\"S002\",\"bindings\":\"X=ℝⁿ with Euclidean topology and Hausdorff separation; K is the arbitrary compact set introduced in S001.\",\"hypothesis_checks\":[\"X carries the Euclidean topology.\",\"Euclidean space is Hausdorff.\",\"K is compact by its arbitrary local declaration.\"]}]}]}}","status":"completed"}],"error":null,"incomplete_details":null,"tools":[{"type":"function","name":"search_mathlib","description":"在固定 mathlib 的 Lean 源码中搜索正则表达式，返回至多 100 行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"query":{"type":"string"}},"required":["query"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_mathlib","description":"读取固定 mathlib 中一个 Mathlib/...lean 文件的指定行。","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start_line":{"type":"integer"},"line_count":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start_line","line_count"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_task_input","description":"Read an explicitly frozen task document by ID; no other local files are accessible.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["id","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_yui","description":"Read declared Yui rules/templates; no tests, historical runs or personal files.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"start":{"type":"integer"},"end":{"type":"integer"}},"required":["path","start","end"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_artifact","description":"Check a JSON artifact against the explicit stage contract; this is not automatic mathematical certification.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_artifact","description":"Submit a JSON artifact after its stage checks.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["artifact_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"report_obstacle","description":"Report exact status, location, explanation, basis, partial_progress. SUBSTANTIVE_GAP or SUSPECTED_GAP stops for an actual unsupported mathematical implication; give its premises, conclusion and mathematical grounds. SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE or INPUT_CONFLICT stops for a real source-access/original-input obstacle. Ordinary unfinished drafting, source registration or format work must use TASK_INCOMPLETE: this records progress without ending the stage; continue the actual work. Difficulty or artifact incompletion alone is not a mathematical gap.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"obstacle_json":{"type":"string"}},"required":["obstacle_json"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"check_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of check_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"submit_draft","description":"Preferred structured-object form of submit_artifact: provide artifact as an actual JSON object, not an escaped JSON string. Same complete validation and acceptance scope.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"artifact":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true}},"required":["artifact"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"probe_library","description":"Query a proved Mathlib theorem and its exact signature/axioms in the offline sandbox. Returns located evidence for an M source; the mathematical statement and applicability still require review.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"id":{"type":"string"},"declaration":{"type":"string"},"module":{"type":"string"}},"required":["id","declaration","module"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false},{"type":"function","name":"read_draft","description":"Read a JSON pointer in your own same-stage candidate after an actual structural check. No other file/stage is accessible; choose a narrow pointer for large objects.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"candidate":{"type":"integer"},"pointer":{"type":"string"}},"required":["candidate","pointer"],"additionalProperties":false},"output_schema":null,"strict":false}],"tool_choice":"auto","parallel_tool_calls":false,"prompt_cache_key":"4e7fc770-8091-4dfe-ab30-4b825a3d6026","prompt_cache_retention":"24h","text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"low"},"top_p":0.98,"top_logprob